1
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:09,333
Space is a lonely town

2
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:12,666
The American Astronaut is a action, comedy, science
fiction film directed by Cory McAbee.

3
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Samual Curtis's first mission in this bizarre science fiction musical
comedy requires him to take a cat to a saloon on an asteroid.

4
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:19,333
There, he meets his former dance partner (the Blueberry Pirate) and collects
his payment: a device capable of producing a Real Live Girl.

5
00:25:16,666 --> 00:25:22,666
Including music by alternative rock group The Billy Nayer Show, this
film began life as a live show with a loyal following.

6
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Blueberry Pirate, played by Joshua Taylor.

7
00:35:23,333 --> 00:35:29,333
The Boy Who Actually Saw a Woman's Breast, played by Greg Russell Cook.

8
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
Professor Hess, played by Rocco Sisto.

9
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
The Silverminer, played by Cory McAbee.

10
00:50:33,333 --> 00:50:39,333
Bodysuit, played by James Ransone.

11
00:55:36,666 --> 00:55:42,666
Cloris, played by Annie Golden.

12
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
The American Astronaut is a 2001 space Western musical
film directed by and starring Cory McAbee.

13
01:05:43,333 --> 01:05:49,333
The film is set in a fictitious past, in which space
travel is pioneered by roughnecks.

14
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
The film was released on DVD in the spring of 2005.

15
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
The band Billy Nayer Show, helmed by McAbee, wrote
and performed the film's soundtrack.

16
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
The film explores themes of breast, space western, astronaut.

17
01:25:56,666 --> 01:26:02,666
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
